## Rules and AUDIT

`docs/rules/` holds the core — `standard.md`, `documentation.md`, `git.md`, `cli.md`,
`dotnet.md` — and `{{APP_NAME}}.md`, which carries this repository's own rules and its
overrides of the core. `{{APP_NAME}}.md` wins on conflict; within the core `dotnet.md`
wins over `standard.md`.

Every core file binds. What differs between them is when they are read, not whether they
apply: a file left unread because the work looked unrelated to it is a rule broken by
default.

**Always, before implementing any change**, read these three in order:

1. `docs/rules/standard.md` — design, comments, testing, specifications, and the AUDIT procedure
2. `docs/rules/dotnet.md` — the .NET rules
3. `docs/rules/{{APP_NAME}}.md` and `docs/specs/{{APP_NAME}}.md`

**Additionally, whenever the work matches a row, read that file too** — this is not
optional and not covered by the three above:

| Work being done | Also read |
|---|---|
| The application being changed exposes a command-line interface (a console application, or a GUI application that accepts command-line options) | `docs/rules/cli.md` |
| Creating, changing, moving, renaming, archiving, or deleting any document | `docs/rules/documentation.md` |
| Any Git write operation or PR operation — commit, branch, push, PR creation, update, or merge | `docs/rules/git.md` |
| The change requires behavior `docs/specs/{{APP_NAME}}.md` does not cover (spec-first applies) | the Specifications section of `docs/rules/standard.md`, before implementing |

- **When transitioning from a plan to implementation**, re-read this file (root and any nested `AGENTS.md` covering the work area) and the rule files named above, so all rules are loaded before code is written
- **Before reporting an implementation task as complete**, run the AUDIT procedure at the end of `docs/rules/standard.md`
- `docs/rules/standard.md`, `docs/rules/documentation.md`, `docs/rules/git.md`, `docs/rules/cli.md`, and `docs/rules/dotnet.md` are managed by dev-standards — never edit them; repository- and application-specific rules go in `docs/rules/{{APP_NAME}}.md`

## Commands

| Purpose | Command |
|---------|---------|
| Format | `dotnet format {{APP_NAME}}.slnx` |
| Format check (must pass before completion) | `dotnet format {{APP_NAME}}.slnx --verify-no-changes` |
| Build | `dotnet build {{APP_NAME}}/{{APP_NAME}}.csproj -c Release` |
| Test | `dotnet test {{APP_NAME}}.Tests/{{APP_NAME}}.Tests.csproj` |
| Full build (format gate → tests → publish) | `build/Menu.bat` (interactive) or `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/Build.ps1` |
| Installer | `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/Installer.ps1` |

## Directory Layout

### `{{APP_NAME}}/`

The main project. Contains all application source code.

### `{{APP_NAME}}.Tests/`

xUnit test project.

### `build/`

Build scripts and installer configuration.

- `Build.ps1` runs the configuration-file check, format verification (`dotnet format --verify-no-changes`), and tests, then publishes {{APP_NAME}} to `build/{{APP_NAME}}/`. All three gates must pass before publish proceeds
- `Installer.ps1` invokes Inno Setup (ISCC.exe) on `Setup_{{APP_NAME}}.iss`; requires `build/{{APP_NAME}}/{{APP_NAME}}.exe` to exist. Before running ISCC it reads `<Version>` from `Directory.Build.props`, injects it via `/DMyAppVersion`, and — if `CHANGELOG.md` exists — verifies it contains a heading for the current version (fails otherwise). The version and CHANGELOG rules are `docs/rules/dotnet.md` VERSION
- Output directories: `build/{{APP_NAME}}/` (publish output) and `build/Installer/` (installer package), both gitignored (rules: `docs/rules/dotnet.md` OUTPUT)

### `docs/`

All non-source documents, placed in role-based subfolders (`rules/`, `adr/`, `specs/`,
`guides/`, `references/`, `investigations/`, `notes/`, `plans/`, `inbox/`, `archive/`).
Before creating, changing, moving, renaming, archiving, or deleting any document — or
when unsure where one belongs — read `docs/rules/documentation.md` (also distributed
in this repository) first; it defines placement, naming, and front matter.

- `docs/rules/` — rule bodies: `standard.md`, `documentation.md`, `git.md`, `cli.md` + `dotnet.md` (managed by dev-standards) and `{{APP_NAME}}.md` (application rules)
- `docs/specs/{{APP_NAME}}.md` — the {{APP_NAME}} specification: what it does
- `docs/adr/` — Architecture Decision Records; retired ADRs move to `docs/adr/archive/`
- `docs/plans/` and `docs/archive/plans/` — working area for plans, gitignored (`docs/rules/documentation.md`, `docs/plans/`)

